Now I need to understand the vulnerability. The crash says "Stack-buffer-overflow READ" in `ot::Message::Write` -> `ot::Message::Append` -> `ot::Mle::Mle::AppendNetworkData`. 

Looking at `FillNetworkDataTlv`:
```cpp
void Mle::FillNetworkDataTlv(NetworkDataTlv &aTlv, bool aStableOnly)
{
    uint8_t length = sizeof(NetworkDataTlv) - sizeof(Tlv); // sizeof( NetworkDataTlv::mNetworkData )
    Get<NetworkData::Leader>().GetNetworkData(aStableOnly, aTlv.GetNetworkData(), length);
    aTlv.SetLength(length);
}
```

The `NetworkDataTlv` is allocated on the stack in `AppendNetworkData`. The `NetworkDataTlv` has a fixed size. But `GetNetworkData` writes into `aTlv.GetNetworkData()` which is the value portion of the TLV. The `length` variable is set to `sizeof(NetworkDataTlv) - sizeof(Tlv)` which is the size of the `mNetworkData` array inside `NetworkDataTlv`.

